# Build context for apps/api/Dockerfile (NestJS + Prisma) and Dockerfile.web (Next.js). Both build from the repository root, so every workspace
# package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml must stay in the context (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` checks all importers). Everything listed here is either
# rebuilt inside the image, never read by a build, or must never reach an image layer (secrets, local databases, VCS metadata).

# Dependencies and build output: always reinstalled/rebuilt in the builder stage for the image's own OS and libc.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.next-*
**/out
**/.turbo
**/.swc
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache

# Prisma: the client is generated inside the image (musl engine); local engines, SQLite files and query logs never belong in a layer.
**/node_modules/.prisma
**/prisma/*.db
**/prisma/*.db-journal

# Secrets and local environment. Committed examples stay. Nothing secret is ever a build input (ADR 0055).
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.npmrc.local
**/.seed-*.json

# Version control, CI, editor and agent metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.gitleaks.toml
.gitleaksignore
.github
.agents
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Tests, coverage and reports produced locally (CI runs tests outside the image).
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
clone-certification-evidence
staging-migration-evidence

# Not read by any build: documentation, infrastructure, security inventories, logs and local data.
docs
infra
security
**/*.log
**/dump.rdb
**/.vercel
**/.terraform
Dockerfile.web
apps/api/Dockerfile
